Then connect using the Jenkins server IP:

ssh root@<JENKINS_SERVER_IP>

Password:

S3curePass
2. Update the apt package information

On the Jenkins server:

apt update

Then check whether Jenkins is available:

apt-cache policy jenkins

If a Jenkins candidate is shown, install it with apt:

apt install -y jenkins
3. Start Jenkins using service

The task specifically requires service, so use:

service jenkins start

Check it:

service jenkins status

You want to see something similar to:

Active: active (running)

You can also verify that Jenkins is listening:

ss -lntp | grep 8080
4. If service jenkins start times out

Follow the task's instruction exactly:

service jenkins status

Then:

cat /var/log/jenkins/jenkins.log

For a more useful view of the latest entries:

tail -50 /var/log/jenkins/jenkins.log

Commonly, Jenkins may simply need more time to initialise. Don't repeatedly restart it immediately; inspect the log first.

